---
/** UK cookies notice (PECR), Glasgow Phase 2. Describes only what the site does today: no cookies
 *  that need consent are set; Cloudflare Web Analytics (cookie-free) is disclosed (owner decision 2026-10-23). With a GA4 id (owner 2026-11-24) the
 *  text says Google Analytics cookies are set only after "Accept" in the banner, and offers "Cookie settings" to change the choice; without one it
 *  says nothing is set. BaseLayout loads GA4 only after opt-in. Not legal advice. */
import { siteConfig } from '../../../lib/site-config';
---
<article class="prose">
  <h1>Cookies</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated {siteConfig.ga4MeasurementId ? 'November' : 'October'} 2026.</em></p>

  {siteConfig.ga4MeasurementId ? (
    <>
      <p>{siteConfig.siteName} asks before it sets any analytics cookie. We would like to use Google Analytics (GA4) to count
      visits and see which pages are read. It is switched off until you press <strong>Accept</strong> in the cookie banner; if you
      press <strong>Decline</strong>, or do not answer, it is not loaded and no Google Analytics cookie is set. After Accept, Google
      Analytics sets the cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_{siteConfig.ga4MeasurementId.replace(/^G-/, '')}</code>, which Google lets
      last up to two years. We do not set any advertising cookies.</p>

      <p>You can change your choice at any time:
      <button type="button" class="linklike" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</button>. This opens the banner again. If you
      change to Decline, Google Analytics is not loaded on your next page view and its cookies are removed from this site. Your
      choice is kept in your browser only, not sent to us.</p>
    </>
  ) : (
    <p>{siteConfig.siteName} does not set any analytics or advertising cookies, so there is no cookie banner and
    nothing for you to accept or refuse.</p>
  )}

  <p>We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to measure page views and page performance. It is cookie-free and does not
  track you between sites. Our lawful basis is legitimate interests; see our
  <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a> for details.</p>

  <p>Cloudflare, our hosting provider, may use a small number of strictly necessary cookies to keep the site
  secure and running smoothly. These are exempt from the consent requirement in the Privacy and Electronic
  Communications Regulations and are not used to track you across other sites.</p>

  <p>Your browser's local storage may hold display preferences such as light or dark mode. These stay on your
  device and are not sent to us.</p>

  <p>If we ever add advertising, or any {siteConfig.ga4MeasurementId ? 'other ' : ''}analytics that uses cookies or tracks you, we will ask for
  your consent before any such cookie is set, make refusing as easy as accepting, and update this page first.</p>

  <p>Questions? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>. See also our <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>.</p>
</article>

<style>
.prose { max-width: 36rem; }
.prose p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
</style>
